course: dictionary
lesson: 8731
title: Serbian: a word about a place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Serbian is an adjective when it describes something from Serbia, such as Serbian food or the Serbian flag. It starts with a capital letter because it comes from a place name. Serbia is a country in south-east Europe, and its capital is Belgrade.
explain: The same word can also name a person. A Serbian is someone from Serbia, and the plural is Serbians. Serbian can also name a language, so you might study Serbian at school.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Languages are written in different scripts, such as the Latin alphabet, Cyrillic, Arabic, Devanagari and Chinese characters, and Serbian can be written in both Cyrillic and Latin letters.» The word both tells you Serbian uses two alphabets, not one.
fact: «Serbian» means from or to do with Serbia, a country in south-east Europe.
fact: Serbia is in the Balkans, and its capital city is Belgrade.
fact: A Serbian is a person from Serbia, also called a Serb.
fact: Serbian is also a language, and it can be written in Cyrillic or Latin letters.
fact: Serbia is landlocked, which means it has no sea coast; it lies on the River Danube.
exercise: The text says «Serbian food» is popular at the school fair. Serbian food comes from which country? | Italy | Greece | *Serbia | Norway
exercise: What is a Serbian? | *A person from Serbia | A river in Europe | A city in Italy | A type of bread
exercise: The text says «Serbian can be written in both Cyrillic and Latin letters.» What does both tell you? | Serbian has no alphabet | *Serbian can use two alphabets | Only one alphabet is allowed | Serbian is written with numbers
test: Which city is the capital of Serbia? | Paris | Novi Sad | Zagreb | *Belgrade
test: Serbia is landlocked. What does that mean? | It is in Asia | *It has no sea coast | It is an island | It has a big sea coast
exam: In «the Serbian flag», what word class is Serbian? | *adjective | adverb | verb | noun
